##! Please refer to the documentation at
##! https://coreruleset.org/docs/development/regex_assembly/.

##! Rule 944160: Malformed Base64 padding (Java4Shell)
##!
##! Detects long Base64 / Base64url tokens whose `=` padding is invalid.
##! Java4Shell is an out-of-bounds heap write in the HotSpot x86-64
##! AVX-512 VBMI Base64 decoder intrinsic. A miscomputed output mask in the
##! tail handling is triggered by padding characters. The published trigger
##! is 64 `A` characters followed by a single `=` (128 `A` + `=` on OpenJDK 17).
##!
##! Valid Base64 can only end in `=` as `xx==` or `xxx=` after full 4-char
##! groups, so the rule matches every other combination and does not match
##! correctly padded data (e.g. Base64-encoded zero bytes).
##!
##! The expression is RE2 compatible: no lookarounds. The token boundaries
##! are consumed as characters instead (start of input or a non-Base64
##! character on the left; end of input or a non-Base64, non-`=` character
##! on the right).
##!
##! Ref: https://calif.io/java4shell

##! Base64 (`+/`) and Base64url (`-_`) alphabet
##!> define b64 A-Za-z0-9+/_\-

##!> assemble
  ##! Left boundary: start of input or a non-Base64 character
  ^
  [^{{b64}}]
  ##!=>

  ##! At least 64 Base64 characters, in full 4-character groups
  (?:[{{b64}}]{4}){16,}
  ##!=>

  ##! Invalid remainder / padding combinations
  ##! remainder 0 or 1 character, followed by any number of `=`
  [{{b64}}]?=+
  ##! remainder 2 characters, followed by 1 or at least 3 `=`
  [{{b64}}]{2}=
  [{{b64}}]{2}={3,}
  ##! remainder 3 characters, followed by at least 2 `=`
  [{{b64}}]{3}={2,}
  ##!=>

  ##! Right boundary: end of input or a non-Base64, non-padding character
  [^{{b64}}=]
  $
##!<
